input.length = data.len;
if (id_blob) { if (copy_to_user(input_address, id_blob, data.len)) { ... } }
Reason:
The return value of __sev_do_cmd_locked() and the firmware error code are not checked. If the PSP command fails (e.g., due to an insufficient userspace buffer), the firmware may set `data.len` to a larger required size than the kernel-allocated `id_blob` buffer. The subsequent `copy_to_user()` then reads beyond the allocated buffer, causing a slab-out-of-bounds KASAN error and potential data leak.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (ret || WARN_ON_ONCE(argp->error))
    goto e_free;
Reason:
The added check prevents copying the ID blob to userspace if the command failed (`ret != 0`) or if the firmware reported an error (`argp->error != 0`). This ensures `data.len` is not used for copying when it may have been set to an invalid larger value by the firmware, avoiding the out-of-bounds read. The `WARN_ON_ONCE` catches driver inconsistencies where the command succeeded but the firmware indicates an error.

